### 4E. PAST SIMPLE (सामान्य भूतकाल) — Completed action

**Pattern:** Subject + **(ने)** + Verb root + **आ/ई/ए** (or irregular past form)

| Hindi | Transliteration | Meaning |
|-------|----------------|---------|
| मैंने खाया | **Maine khaayaa** | I ate |
| मैं गया (गयी) | **Main gayaa (gayee)** | I went |
| तुमने क्या किया? | **Tumne kya kiyaa?** | What did you do? |
| उसने बोला | **Usne bolaa** | He/She said |
| हमने देखा | **Humne dekhaa** | We saw |
| वो आया (आयी) | **Vo aayaa (aayee)** | He/She came |
| मैंने पैसे दिए | **Maine paise diye** | I gave money |
| उसने फ़ोन किया | **Usne phone kiyaa** | He/She called |

**ने (ne) Rule:** Use **ने** after subject when verb is transitive (action passes to an object).
- खाना खाया → मैं**ने** खाना खाया (**I** ate food — "I" did the action on "food")
- गया → मैं गया (No ने — "went" has no object)

**Casual sentences:**

| Hindi | Transliteration | Meaning |
|-------|----------------|---------|
| कल क्या किया? | **Kal kya kiyaa?** | What did you do yesterday? |
| मैंने उसे बताया | **Maine use bataayaa** | I told him/her |
| खाना बहुत अच्छा लगा | **Khaanaa bahut achchaa lagaa** | The food was very good |
| पार्टी में बहुत मज़ा आया | **Party mein bahut mazaa aayaa** | Had a lot of fun at the party |
| मैंने गलती कर दी | **Maine galatee kar dee** | I made a mistake |
| वो कुछ नहीं बोला | **Vo kuchh naheen bolaa** | He didn't say anything |
| बस छूट गई | **Bas chhoot gayee** | Missed the bus |
| लाइट चली गई | **Light chalee gayee** | Power went out |

