## 30. PRACTICE EXERCISES

### Translate to Hindi:
1. Where are you going?
2. I am hungry.
3. What time is it?
4. Please give me water.
5. I don't understand.
6. Let's go to the market.
7. He is my friend.
8. The food is very tasty.
9. I will come tomorrow.
10. Don't worry, everything will be fine.

### Answers:
1. तुम कहाँ जा रहे हो? *(Tum kahaan jaa rahe ho?)*
2. मुझे भूख लगी है। *(Mujhe bhookh lagee hai.)*
3. कितने बजे हैं? *(Kitne baje hain?)*
4. मुझे पानी दीजिए। *(Mujhe paanee deejiye.)*
5. मुझे समझ नहीं आया। *(Mujhe samajh naheen aayaa.)*
6. चलो बाज़ार चलते हैं। *(Chalo baazaar chalte hain.)*
7. वो मेरा दोस्त है। *(Vo meraa dost hai.)*
8. खाना बहुत स्वादिष्ट है। *(Khaanaa bahut svaadisht hai.)*
9. मैं कल आऊँगा। *(Main kal aaoongaa.)*
10. चिंता मत करो, सब ठीक हो जाएगा। *(Chintaa mat karo, sab theek ho jaayegaa.)*

---

> **Tips for Learning:**
> - Practice speaking out loud — pronunciation matters more than spelling
> - Start with the **Casual Phrases** section — these are used 90% of the time
> - Gender agreement (masculine/feminine) is the hardest part — keep practicing
> - Watch Hindi movies/shows with subtitles to hear natural pronunciation
> - Use **यार (yaar)** and **भाई (bhaai)** generously — they make conversations feel natural
> - Hindi uses **SOV** (Subject-Object-Verb) order: "मैं खाना खाता हूँ" = "I food eat am"
